  "assumptions": {
    "noise": "Expected 2.9-5.1 micron white-light noise from official online PandExo saved counts and variances, including reset duty cycle, read noise and background. J-normalized Phoenix spectrum and accepted PID10786 detector setup. No extra noise floor or correlated noise. Engine/refdata version is not exposed by online output.",
    "depth": "Photon-weighted flat-throughput blackbody band 2.9-5.1 micron; Tbrightness=1.1*Teq; not atmospheric spectrum or ETC model",
    "geometry": "Fixed circular representative geometry. Dated 2025-08-13 composite archive ratios and a/Rstar; inclinations checked against live NASA default 2026-10-09; periods from accepted PID10786 APT. Composite values can mix literature solutions. No orbit uncertainty or eccentricity recovery.",
    "visit": "Symmetric continuous visit about eclipse, length equals APT total science exposure seconds. Ideal 60-second bins with no gaps; not measured timestamps.",
    "trend": "delta=atan(tan(40 degrees)*(1500 K/Teq)^3). Illustrative radiative/advection scaling inspired by Showman2020; normalization chosen for simulation, not extracted GCM prediction.",
    "science": "Band brightness hot spot longitude, not pressure-specific temperature offset or phase-curve peak; profile-grid screening, not full NUTS validation.",
    "cadence": "Expected noise per60seconds of wall time. Recovery uses ideal continuous 60-second integrated bins, not exact detector timestamps; reset loss is included in noise, not explicitly masked within each model exposure.",
    "primary_ensemble": "Primary expected-noise ensemble: 100 predeclared deterministic trial seeds per target. Seeds derive from master seed 20261009, target index, fixed noise index 0, and trial index. Trial 0 matches the prior one-draw run. No sample selection. The longitude grid step is 0.25 degrees for all six targets."
